@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>How your privacy works · BridgeTogether</PageTitle>

<MudStack Spacing="3">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h4" HtmlTag="h1">How your privacy works</MudText>
    <MudText>
        This is a plain-language summary of how BridgeTogether handles what you write. It is not
        a legal privacy notice; that will be published before the app opens to the public.
    </MudText>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-4" Outlined="true">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2">What stays private</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            Your reflections and drafts are visible only to you. Being in a workspace with your partner
            does not give them access to any of it, and we never show it to them automatically.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-4" Outlined="true">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2">What gets shared</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            Only a message you preview and approve is shared, and only with your partner. If you change
            the text after previewing it, you have to approve it again. You can take back a message you
            shared: your partner will no longer see it in the app, although they may already have read it.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-4" Outlined="true">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2">If either of you leaves</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            When either partner leaves the workspace, shared messages stop being visible to the other.
            Your own reflections and drafts stay yours.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-4" Outlined="true">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2">Your controls</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            In <MudLink Href="Account/Manage/PersonalData">Account › Personal data</MudLink> you can download
            everything we hold about you, or delete your account. Deleting erases your reflections, drafts,
            consent history and the messages you shared or received. Your partner keeps their own account
            and their own private data.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-4" Outlined="true">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2">What we never do</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            We don't put what you write into logs, notifications or analytics. We keep records of
            actions, such as "a message was shared", using ids only, for security.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>
</MudStack>
